<speak>Mostly the computer when I want to read properly. The phone is fine for seeing that something has arrived, but not for dealing with a long document. I end up enlarging the page, moving it sideways, then forgetting which paragraph I was reading. On the computer, I can put the document beside my notes. That's much more comfortable. I also have a printer, though I'm trying not to print everything automatically. Otherwise the study starts looking like a second office, which defeats the purpose of being home.</speak>